It is Wednesday after work.
I take the U-Bahn to my neighbourhood.
I walk directly to the repair shop.
My bicycle is there.
The mechanic sees me.
"Hello, Frau Flores," he says.
"Your bicycle is ready."
He fetches the bicycle.
"The brakes work perfectly now," he says.
I test the brakes.
They are really great.
"Thank you very much," I say.
I ride the bicycle to my flat.
The ride is a lot of fun.
Every day I take the U-Bahn to the office.
That is always the same and sometimes a bit boring.
Now the bicycle is repaired.
I will now sometimes ride the bicycle to work.
